Package: DesignComplexSurvival
Type: Package
Title: Simulation-Free Design of Complex Time-to-Event Trials
Version: 0.2.2
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Gosuke", "Homma",
      email = "my.name.is.gosuke@gmail.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6854-5627")
    )
  )
Description: Computes the expected numbers of events, the mean, variance and
    covariance of the log-rank statistic over calendar time, and the power,
    type I error, required number of events, sample size, accrual duration
    and follow-up of two-group time-to-event trials, without patient-level
    simulation. Each group follows a four-state model (progression-free,
    progressed, switched, dead) with piecewise constant intensities, which
    covers progression-free survival, overall survival and treatment
    switching at or after progression, together with piecewise uniform
    accrual, piecewise exponential dropout and group sequential designs with
    efficacy bounds and binding or non-binding futility bounds.
    Progression-free and overall survival can be tested together with a
    group sequential fixed-sequence or Bonferroni procedure, using the joint
    distribution of the two log-rank statistics over calendar time. The
    variance and covariance of the log-rank score under the alternative
    follow Luo et al. (2019) <doi:10.1002/sim.7975>.
